    "result_text": "The implementation is complete. There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented deriving a `timezone` field on the owner, as an IANA name mapped from the locality/region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges, following the existing derived-field conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the owner response schema (after `locality`), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `timezone` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 Added the pinned `REGION_TIMEZONE` table and a public `timezoneForRegion(String region)` helper, colocated with the sibling region/postcode tables so the mapping isn't duplicated. Returns `null` for unknown regions (so the field is absent, matching the \"Absent when the region has no known timezone\" spec).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired a `timezone` `@Mapping` that derives the region from the owner's `customerCode` (the same source as `locality`, keeping them in step) and looks up its timezone.\n\nThe new `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` acceptance test passes (`$.locality` = `NSW`, `$.timezone` = `Australia/Sydney`), and the full suite is green.",
